+
+## Known limitations and open questions
+
+- A single marker listing many sources, for example `[S1, S2, S3, S4, S5, S6]` (22 inner characters), is not recognised because of the 16-character cap the plan sets. The text stays visible in the answer and no alias is validated from it. If models do this in practice, raising `MAX_MARKER_HOLD_CHARS` is a one-line change but delays release of a stray opener in the stream by the same amount. Product owner to confirm 16 is enough once plan 05-08 prompts are measured.
+- Digits are not capped inside an alias, so `[S1234567890123]` is a marker whose alias is simply unknown to the request set and is counted as invalid.
